------------------------------------------------------------
FAITHFUL-PARITY NOTE (states)
------------------------------------------------------------
The web UsageCard is a PURE presentational primitive (its own header: "no hooks,
no API calls, no derived state. Every dynamic value comes in via props"). It has
no fetch/Promise/React-Query, so it has NO loading / error / stale / offline
branch — there is nothing to load, fail, age, or lose connectivity to (its host
owns those). Fabricating that chrome would be silent drift from the source, so —
exactly as the sibling pure primitives MetricCard (0095) / Accordion (0203) — this
surface reproduces only the source's REAL branches and documents the rest:
  • empty   (!hasAnything)   -> friendly empty leaf, never a blank panel.
  • budget  -> headline/right-label/caption + clamped bar (width 0..100) with an
               UNCLAMPED rounded a11y value so over-budget is still announced.
  • bands   -> 3-up adaptive grid, per-band intent ring/tint.
  • details -> KV grid, per-detail value intent.
  • topLists-> breakdown blocks (mono name + tabular value).
  • banner  -> callout, default danger intent + warning glyph.
  • footer  -> primary/secondary x internal(onNavigate)/external(open URL) links.

